shattered-maps-client is the Mapper. Phase 23 made the home page (`#/`, `neutral/`) a viewer and curation tool on the neutral map file (zoom levels, gaps, off-page links, baseline, candidate review into an audited layer file); the classic editor moved from the DslMapper repository without a behaviour change lives on at `#/legacy` with its hexagon (`#/map/...`) and octagon (`#/renderer/...`) views, in `ClassicApp.tsx`, loaded lazily so its global styles do not reach the neutral viewer. The audited map can be exported to the Builder as an .are file (`neutral/components/ExportPanel.tsx`, docs/shattered-maps/builder-export.md); the page never calls the Builder. Two stores on purpose: `state/mapStore` (classic, key `dslmapper.autosave`) and `neutral/state` (keys `shatteredmaps.audited`, `shatteredmaps.review`). docs/shattered-maps/app.md lists what each phase changed. A static single-page app: a container of the dev stack (deploy/shattered-maps-client.Dockerfile, the experimental compose, the edge vhost deploy/nginx/edge-maps.conf, not in the production compose) and `vite` on port 22080 for development. No server, no data volume: the editor keeps its work in the browser.

Two renderers exist on purpose for now: `render/svgExport.ts`, `hexMath.ts` and `octMath.ts` here (the Mapper's own, pinned by `render/seed.test.ts`), and `services/shattered-maps-core/src/render.ts` (derived from this code, with full escaping and rounded numbers). Their text differs, so do not swap one for the other without updating the pin; which one survives is decided in the rework onto the neutral model.

Eleven files start with an `eslint-disable no-explicit-any` line: moved code to be typed with the neutral model, not a licence for new `any`. The lint script allows exactly 5 warnings (the advisory ones listed in app.md); a new warning fails it.

The room form's hooks live in `RoomFormFor`, below the check that the room exists. Do not move them back above `if (!room)`: React's order-of-hooks check fails when a room appears or disappears (`components/RoomForm.test.tsx` covers it).

Hexagon pages: every area has its own origin, so `pages/MapAreaPage` and `MapRoomPage` must filter by `category.areaId` (never draw "all rooms of the floor"); `render/coords.ts` `placeRoom` lays `cx`/`cy` rooms on the octagon view's compass grid (a cube needs only cx and cy: saved documents have no cz), legacy `q`/`r` rooms on the hex lattice. Covered by `pages/hexPages.test.tsx` and `render/geometry.test.ts`.

The saved document uses the localStorage key `dslmapper.autosave` and is read by `state/persist.ts` and `MapProvider`; renaming it would orphan every existing user's work.
